  "response": "To make promptfoo run providers one at a time, you can use the `-j 1` option. This option serializes the evaluation's target calls, meaning one provider and one prompt are evaluated sequentially rather than concurrently. You can run the following command in your terminal:\n\n```bash\npromptfoo eval -j 1\n```\n\nThis setting serializes the target calls, processing each provider and prompt one at a time. However, it's important to note that there's an ordering caveat: test cases marked with `options.runSerially` are executed in a separate partition ahead of the rest, so they do not follow strict test-case order even when using `-j 1`.\n\nAdditionally, model-graded assertions are serialized when grading grouping is active. If it is disabled, a certain level of concurrency, defined by `PROMPTFOO_ASSERTIONS_MAX_CONCURRENCY` (default is 3), can still occur within a single test case.",
